## 1. Overview

In this lab, Splunk Enterprise is deployed as a SIEM solution to collect and centralize security logs from the OPNsense firewall.

The integration allows OPNsense to forward its system and firewall logs to Splunk through remote syslog. These logs can then be searched and analyzed from a centralized interface to monitor network activity and support security investigations.

This lab builds on the previous Suricata IDS deployment and introduces centralized security log management using Splunk.
## 2. Objectives

The objectives of this lab are to:

- Deploy Splunk Enterprise as a SIEM platform.
- Configure Splunk to receive syslog data through UDP.
- Configure OPNsense to forward firewall logs to Splunk.
- Centralize firewall logs for security monitoring.
- Explore how centralized logging supports network security monitoring and incident investigation.
