## 5. Configuration

### 5.1 Splunk Enterprise Configuration

Splunk Enterprise 10.6.1 was installed on the Ubuntu 26.04 LTS virtual machine (192.168.152.132).

After installation, Splunk was initialized with an administrator account and started as a service.

The Splunk Web Interface is accessible through:

`http://192.168.152.132:8000`

**Syslog Input Configuration**

A UDP input was created in Splunk to receive logs forwarded by OPNsense.

| Parameter | Configuration |
|---|---|
| Input Type | UDP |
| Port | 1514 |
| Source Type | syslog |
| Index | main |
| App Context | Search & Reporting |

The UDP input allows Splunk to listen for incoming syslog messages from the OPNsense firewall.

### 5.2 OPNsense Remote Logging Configuration

OPNsense was configured to forward its system and firewall logs to the Splunk server using remote syslog.

The configuration was performed under:

`System → Settings → Logging → Remote`

The following parameters were configured:

| Parameter | Configuration |
|---|---|
| Transport | UDP (4) |
| Applications | Select All |
| Levels | Select All |
| Facilities | Select All |
| Destination Host | 192.168.152.132 |
| Destination Port | 1514 |

This configuration enables OPNsense to transmit its selected system and firewall logs to the Splunk server over UDP port 1514.

### 5.3 Configuration Summary

At this stage, Splunk Enterprise and OPNsense have been configured to support centralized log collection.

The following configuration components are in place:

- Splunk Enterprise installed on Ubuntu Server.
- Splunk administrator account initialized.
- UDP input configured on port 1514.
- Source type set to `syslog`.
- Destination index set to `main`.
- OPNsense remote logging configured to forward logs to the Splunk server.
- Remote syslog communication configured using UDP.

The environment is now configured for centralized collection of OPNsense system and firewall logs.
### 6.1 Verify Log Reception in Splunk

To verify the integration, the following search query was executed in Splunk Search & Reporting:

```spl
index=main sourcetype=syslog
```

**Results:**

Splunk successfully received 3,342 events from the OPNsense firewall.

The collected events contain the following information:

| Field | Observed Value |
|---|---|
| Source IP | 192.168.152.130 |
| Source | udp:1514 |
| Sourcetype | syslog |
| Index | main |
| Log Source | filterlog |
| Interfaces | em0 and em1 |

The search results confirm that OPNsense firewall logs are successfully forwarded to Splunk through UDP port 1514.

**Status:** Successful log collection.

